How this flow works now:
 * Network drops during approval.
 * System retries automatically 1st, 2nd, 3rd, 4th time... telling the user to "Please wait".
 * After the 5th failure, it stops trying.
 * It changes the database status directly back to P.
 * Because the status is P, the batch instantly reappears in the Checker's Dashboard. 6. A notification arrives saying: "Execution failed after maximum retries... The request is again available in the queue. Please try to approve it again."
 * The Checker simply clicks "Approve" one more time, and the whole system tries fresh!
